<title>USA: U.S. chain store sales up 0.7 pct - BTM/Schroders.</title>
<headline>U.S. chain store sales up 0.7 pct - BTM/Schroders.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales rose 0.7 percent in the week ended December 14 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were up 4.2 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index was up 0.8 percent from the prior month.</p>
<p>&quot;With Christmas just eight days away, retailers are using phrases such as, 'solid but not great,' 'a little better than might be expected,' and 'terrific business so far,' to describe the 1996 Christmas selling season,&quot; a BTM report said.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
